[kellen4]: I think it is because I have spec.cert.webSecretName set, both 
https://gitlab.com/ongresinc/stackgres/-/blob/main/stackgres-k8s/src/operator/src/main/java/io/stackgres/operator/conciliation/factory/config/webconsole/WebConsoleGrafanaIntegartionConfigMap.java

and 

https://gitlab.com/ongresinc/stackgres/-/blob/main/stackgres-k8s/src/operator/src/main/java/io/stackgres/operator/conciliation/factory/config/webconsole/AdminuiNginxConfigMap.java

use it for naming their configmaps:
```java
  public static String name(StackGresConfig config) {
    return ResourceUtil.resourceName(
        config.getSpec().getCert() != null
        && config.getSpec().getCert().getWebSecretName() != null
        ? config.getSpec().getCert().getWebSecretName()
            : WebConsoleDeployment.name(config) + "-nginx");
  }
```
and
```java
  public static String name(StackGresConfig config) {
    return ResourceUtil.resourceName(
        config.getSpec().getCert() != null
        && config.getSpec().getCert().getWebSecretName() != null
        ? config.getSpec().getCert().getWebSecretName()
            : WebConsoleDeployment.name(config) + "-grafana-integration");
  }
```

[kellen4]: Can confirm, deleting spec.cert.webSecretName causes two separate ConfigMaps to be generated and the AdminUI works as expected.

