[teoincontatto]: This is related to a [common problem](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/99003) about migrating resources from non-SSA to SSA.

A dirty workaround to this situation is to [remove the field managers](https://github.com/fluxcd/kustomize-controller/issues/486#issuecomment-966418532).

[teoincontatto]: After trying the above workaround I saw that some fields ended up not being deleted

[teoincontatto]: Seems like Server Side Apply is broken for secrets when using `.stringData` field to store secret value in plain format. The manager that set key-pairs in such field becomes the owner of those fields under `.stringData` but the resource get stored with only the `.data` field (with encoded value). When you remove any field from the `.stringData` it will not be removed by Kubernetes from the `.data` field breaking some StackGres use cases:

* Pod can not be restarted if the cluster has been created from a backup and the backup has been removed.
* Changing storage in backup config prevent backup from working due to the inconsistencies in configuration (any env var that is not removed from the secret).

To make secret to work with SSA I will change the Kubernetes client implementation in order to always set the `.data` by encoding values of the `.stringData` and removing it if set.

